This temporal structure is critical for the causal model. The dramatic acceleration occurs after the late 1970s, coinciding with major structural changes in the U.S. economy including deindustrialization, agricultural mechanization, and the shift to a service-based economy. A first-pass causal model should therefore examine the temporal structure $1945 \rightarrow 1960 \rightarrow 1975 \rightarrow 1985 \rightarrow 1995 \rightarrow 2005 \rightarrow 2015 \rightarrow 2026$ rather than comparing endpoints.

