3. Institutionalized populations. NHANES excludes institutionalized individuals (e.g., nursing homes, prisons), which may affect estimates for older age groups and certain demographic subgroups.
4. BMI as a proxy. BMI does not distinguish between fat mass and lean mass, nor does it capture fat distribution. These limitations are discussed in detail in Appendix B.

